=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed existing codebase:
- internal/api/telemetry_sessions.go: TelemetrySessionTracker with RecoverSessions (restores
  in-memory tracking state for recent open sessions) and ValidateRecoveredSessions (auto-closes
  stale/completed sessions based on SignalStore state).
- internal/database/signal_log_reader.go: SnapshotAt, SnapshotBetween, SignalTrace,
  DriveAggregates, ChargeAggregates, RegenEnergy — no LatestTimestamp yet.
- internal/database/drive_repo.go: GetStale(ctx, cutoff) returns drives WHERE end_ts IS NULL
  AND start_ts < cutoff. CompleteWithTx, PartialUpdateWithTx for closing drives.
- internal/database/charging_repo.go: GetStale(ctx, cutoff) returns charges WHERE end_ts IS NULL
  AND start_ts < cutoff. CompleteWithTx, PartialUpdateWithTx for closing charges.
- cmd/teslasync/main.go: Session recovery sequence at lines 237-243: RecoverSessions →
  ValidateRecoveredSessions → StartBufferDrains. SignalLogReader not yet wired.
- SetSignalLogReader exists on TelemetrySessionTracker but was never called from main.go.

=== REASONING ===
Design:
1. LatestTimestamp on SignalLogReader: Simple MAX(created_at) query with timeout.
2. RecoverIncompleteSessions on TelemetrySessionTracker:
   - Requires signalLogReader (returns early if nil).
   - Uses GetStale(ctx, now) to find ALL open drives/charges (start_ts < now covers everything).
   - Skips sessions already tracked in activeDrives/activeCharges (handled by RecoverSessions).
   - For each remaining open session: checks LatestTimestamp, skips if < 5 min stale.
   - Stale sessions completed using SnapshotAt + DriveAggregates/ChargeAggregates.
   - No signals at all → still completes with minimal data (best-effort, don't leave open forever).
3. completeRecoveredDrive / completeRecoveredCharge: Simplified versions of completeDriveLocked /
   completeChargeLocked that operate on DB models + signal_log snapshots (no in-memory streamingDrive).
   Replicates the signal_log enrichment sections (unit-aware distance, battery, temperature,
   energy, speed/power aggregates, regen). Sets ended_status="recovered".
4. Wiring: main.go creates SignalLogReader, calls SetSignalLogReader, then RecoverIncompleteSessions
   runs after RecoverSessions + ValidateRecoveredSessions but before StartBufferDrains.

=== CHANGES ===
Files changed:
1. internal/database/signal_log_reader.go
   - Added LatestTimestamp(ctx, vehicleID) (time.Time, error)
   - Returns MAX(created_at) from signal_log for the vehicle
   - Returns zero time when no signals exist

2. internal/api/telemetry_sessions.go
   - Added const staleSessionThreshold = 5 * time.Minute
   - Added RecoverIncompleteSessions(ctx) method
   - Added completeRecoveredDrive(ctx, drive, startSnap, endSnap, endTs) method
   - Added completeRecoveredCharge(ctx, charge, startSnap, endSnap, endTs) method

3. cmd/teslasync/main.go
   - Created signalLogReader via database.NewSignalLogReader(db)
   - Wired via sessionTracker.SetSignalLogReader(signalLogReader)
   - Added sessionTracker.RecoverIncompleteSessions(ctx) call after ValidateRecoveredSessions

